I have succesfully installed RH7.1 using the 2.2.18 based MILO on a XL266.
In general I think this version is more stable than the older versions. I
sometimes have to reboot when milo starts and give me a garbled screen. This
may haveto do with the S3 Virge 4Mb PCI video card I use. I have Linload and
Milo in a DOS partition and on floppy. Both work most of the time fine.
 
Egbert Jan
Dutch Hobby Computer Club
 

-----Original Message-----
From: James L [mailto:wokboy@hotmail.com]
Sent: zondag 26 augustus 2001 3:52
To: axp-list@redhat.com
Subject: Milo for XL366 trying to install RH7.1 


Does anyone have a working version of Milo 2.2.x for an Alpha XL366?
 
I am trying to install RedHat7.1 on my Alpha XL366.  When I boot from the
Kernel disk included with RH7.1 it seems to get stuck in a rebooting loop
with Milo 2.0.35 which was what I was using with RH6.2.
 
I tried using the kernel disk from 7.0 and then the ramdisk image from 7.1
this allowed me to install RH7.1 seemingly without problem but when I tried
to boot the first time, still with milo 2.0.35 the same rebooting loop
happens...it deosn't seem to load...the last thing i see is 
 
---------------------------------------------------------
 
then reboot.
 
I have tried the MILO binaries from www.suse.de/~stepan
<http://www.suse.de/~stepan>  of 2.2.17.and 2.2.18 but both seem to hang
when switching to PALCode. I haven't managed to get MILO compiled.
 
Has anyone managed to get RH7.1 installed on an XL366 or any XLT?
 
Some tips would be appreciated
 
Cheers,
 
James
 



 
