Some other interesting wrinkles that came to my (twisted) mind:

1)
Capellas promised to "turn around the company" or quit.

Seems he did neither. Instead he trimmed it for sale to HP, then took a 
position at HP.

Breach of trust, at least in how I see it. Possible fraud?

2)
So this is the REAL explanation for the Alpha fiasco. HP did not want 
Alpha. Already have RISC chip and have a pre-existing deal with Intel for 
Itanium..
So, I wonder if  the USA FTC will review the actions of Intel, HP and Compaq?
It is obvious that HP had a hand in this long ago..

3)
And on the positive side it seems that Compaq was being nice to their 
employees and landing them a job at Intel, rather than HP letting them go..


