Umm  the vast majority of Alphas are PCI based. There are a few models that did
do AGP
like the Nautilus and I've had an AGP voodoo3 in one working at one point.

> If I were to grab a new video card, any recommendations for decent perf?  Not
> gaming, just really want an MS alternative...and wish I had gotten into Alpha
> long before the corporate technology slaughtering began.

I get good milage out of voodoo3 cards even if the DRI interface for it will
only work in 16bit and not 24.
Other intresting options that will operate with DRI would be most mga cards
(Matrox) and radeon boards. The ATI rage 128 should also work.

DRI support is a BIG win. Try and get a card that supports it

Phil
