Hi all,

I was wondering if there's a antivirus scanner available for Alpha Linux. I use
an AS200 with RedHat7.1 as a mail server and fileserver and I would like to
scan incomming mail (maybe even incomming http data too) for viruses. I'm using
qmail an I got the addon for using any command line scanner for incomming mail.

The problem is that most AV scanners are just compiled for Linux on intel
machines (if they're avaiable for Linux at all).

Of course free scanners would be prefered (i'm a student - can't spend $$$$ on
top products, although a small fee can be acceptible). 

If there isn't a scanner compiled for axp - is it possible to use an emulator.
How about performance/security. I heard that some years ago you had to use such
an emulator to get netscape running but I don't the name. Can you give me some
pointers?

Thanks, Gregor


