-> FAT: bogus logical sector size 24716
-> FAT: bogus logical sector size 24716
-> Kernel Panic:  VFS:  Unable to mount root fs on 08:02

I'm not sure about what is happening with you, but it seems
that you're using FAT filesystem!!!

You have to use a BSD partition table in order to use aboot
and you'll need to compile your kernel to support it.

regards, nelson




