Greetings,

About a year and a half ago, I got a "developer's special" UP1000 
machine from DCG, now part of Atipa.  I got it with a Voodoo3 AGP.  It 
worked fine (didn't try X though, nor DRI :-) until our group moved some 
things around the room, so it got picked up and put down twice, but not 
dropped.

Now the power light and fan come on, and the startup noise is there, but 
nothing on the screen.

The machine has Debian installed, and I haven't figured out how to make 
it auto-boot, I have to load the PAL code from a floppy and boot from 
there every time.  So I would like to see the screen, I don't trust 
myself to type blind when I don't even remember exactly what it's 
supposed to say back to me.  Perhaps I should have written down exactly 
what I type to boot it *before* this happened, so I could at least ssh 
in. :-(

So in any case, I have no idea where to start troubleshooting. 
 Everything seems to be seated just fine, including the Voodoo3.  Atipa 
hasn't returned my two phone calls...

Any ideas?

TIA,
-- 

-Adam P.

