You can use the CD-ROM to boot, just pass the kernel your root
filesystem. Something like:

P00>>boot dka0 -fi kernels/generic.gz -fl "root=/dev/sd2 single"

of course you'll need to check those parameters.

Then once you in single user mode you can you swrteboot manually:

swriteboot /dev/sda /boot/bootlx

--rdp

