If you setup your disklabel to emulate a TRU64 installation, (i.e. partition
c being the entire disk ) you will have to boot up from your CD, then issue
the  "swriteboot -f3" to force aboot to be written into the 3rd partition.
If the first few blocks of your drive aren't part of a partition, the
standard install will write aboot to your hard drive for you, but it won't
write it out if it thinks those blocks may have some data on them ( if it is
in a partition. )

HTH...

T 
