Hi,

We have an UP2000 with only one 666MHz processor and one internal
harddisk. Today, the 430W power supply died and I've replaced it with a
spare 300W power supply. Now the problem is that the machine does not
start up most of the time. What happens is that everything is powered up,
including all fans, CPU fans, the harddisk, CD-ROM is spinning up but I do
not get any video and no signs that machine is booting. When I press the
"Reset" button, I see that the (IDE) CD-ROM is being reset because the LED
blinks but still no video.

Now when I toggle the power several times, I occasionally get it running
and get a video signal and everything behaves just fine. But most of the
time I turn it on, I don't get a video signal.

Question: Anybody seen this? Can this be the result of the power supply
being too weak? Do I really need a 400+ Watt power supply for a UP2000 ?

Thanks // Tom
