With regards to your message at 10:44 PM 9/24/01, Amal D'Silva. Where you 
stated:
>Does anyone have information (preferably quantitative) on how DDR cache 
>fares against Late-write cache ? Specifically, API's 833 MHz CPUs have 4MB 
>DDR cache against the 750 MHz /8MB Late write. So in general, which CPU 
>would give better performance ?
>Thanks,
>
>Amal


Tough to answer as a generality.
8MB cache assures a better chance of a cache "hit" where things might fit 
better, whereas DDR cache, being faster, helps performance overall.
Part of the reason 750MHz had such large cache was that it was running RAM 
at a lower clock rate than 667 or 833. 75MHz for 750, versus 83MHz for 667 
and 833. Needed bigger cache to show performance resulting from higher 
clock than 667.
Probably why Compaq did not ship 750's.


