Hi,

Today I got the replacement power supply. It was even stronger (550W) than
the old one and has also got the additional Power Connecter (Old style,
Baby-AT) for the Motherboard. After replacing the Power supply, though,
the problems remained and the machine did not start most of the time.

After a detailled inspection I found out that one of the CPU-A fans was
not running and hence the "Power GOOD" Led was not lit. This kept the
machine from starting. As I only got one CPU anyway I've just replaced the
faulty fan with one of the CPU-B fans and all is well now.

Tom
