The psacct-6.3.2-5 rpm for RH7.1 alpha seems to have a serious bug in
the date/time field. Example:

| $ lastcomm | head
| sh                 myuserid    ??         0.07 secs Fri Dec 10 21:02
| stty               myuserid    ??         0.03 secs Fri Jan 15 06:21
| sed                myuserid    ??         0.07 secs Fri Dec 10 21:02
| ls                 myuserid    ??         0.28 secs Sun Jan 26 14:32
| find               myuserid    ??         0.57 secs Wed Mar 20 04:19
| sh                 myuserid    ??         0.08 secs Sun Nov 15 07:46
| stty               myuserid    ??         0.04 secs Thu Oct 21 21:21
| sh                 myuserid    ??         0.10 secs Sat Jan 29 20:41
| comm               myuserid    ??       195.01 secs (null)          
| wc                 myuserid    ??         0.04 secs Mon Feb 21 12:47
| $ 

All the commands in the above example were executed during the last
minute, and not at the time that's printed. With this bug, the
"lastcomm" command is pretty useless to me. Note the "last" command
doesn't show this bug.

Anyone knows a patch or a work-around?

Thanks for your help,


