Dear Alpha-Linux users !

(This is a re-post, because yesterday's sending seems to be lost.)

As some of you may remember, I want to upgrade the graphics card 
on my AS200 ("Avanti") from the original Digital TGA. 
Following the recommendations, I managed to get a Matrox Millennium 
G200 SD ("G2+/MSDP/8I" - the PCI version, with 8 MB of RAM). 
My machine is running the SuSE 7.0 AXP distribution (kernel 2.2.16), 
it boots via ARC (3.5-13), LinuxLoader 1.5, and Milo 2.0.35-c5.6.

My intention was to do the upgrade in these steps:
-) Change "initdefault" to 2 (no graphics), 
   do a "full backup" to tape, halt the machine.
-) Exchange the graphic cards.
-) Boot into text mode, install the X server for the new card, 
   and configure it.

However, on booting with the new card I get a totally blank 
(= black) screen; neither the ARC messages nor anything later 
does show up, nor do I hear the normal disk activity (when waiting).
I am sure I inserted the card correctly and did not touch / loosen 
anything else, also I fitted the terminal plug firmly.

When I use the "ScreenManager" feature of my monitor (Eizo FlexScan 
F730), it shows both horizontal and vertical frequency to be "0.0" 
immediately after power-on - this was the same for the old card.

In the ARC phase, the old card produced 37.7 kHz / 72.6 Hz, 
the new one sends 36.9 kHz / 82.2 Hz (according to ScreenManager) 
(which to me implies the connections are ok). 
This is well within the monitor limits (30 - 115 kHz / 50 - 160 Hz), 
also, the numbers are shown in black (errors should display in red), 
however, the screen is totally black (except for ScreenManager).

Using the reset button does not change anything.

After changing back to the old card, the machine (auto-) boots
correctly.

Obviously, my questions are:

1) Is anybody using the Matrox Millennium G200 card with an AS200 
   and/or the ARC console (which version)? 
   Any problems, tricks, experiences?

2) Should I try to upgrade the ARC version (my version 3.5-13 
   mentions the year 1993) - chances of improvement? 
   To which version - newest, or something older "known good"? 
   I have never done this before - is it risky or safe? 

3) We also run Tru64 machines, and I have the "firmware update" CDs - 
   can I use them to update the AS200 / ARC, or must I use the 
   FTP download / floppy approach?

4) My understanding was that all cards support some standard VGA 
   text mode upon power-up - why are there ARC text problems? 
   Is there any chance to influence ARC in this phase?

   I also thought ARC uses some "common denominator", low resolution - 
   why do the cards produce different frequencies in this phase? 
   (To me, 82 Hz vertical seems surprisingly high in a boot phase.)

5) Or is my only chance to change to SRM (which I would like to 
   avoid, because AIUI this means to re-partition the disk 
   and hence re-install everything)?

6) Any archive to search? www.alphalinux.org seems unreachable, 
   and the copy at "linuxalpha" does not have all internal links 
   changed, so searching is quite painful. 
   All I found was a message dated Thu Nov 18 1999 (author Robb 
   Romans (robb@killsoft.com), title "Re: PC164 and Matrox G200?") 
   stating "Works ok on mine with either SRM or ARC." 
   (I would be glad if I could say the same.)

7) Any other hints / proposals / info needed?

Thank you for any help. 
If I get any mail answers off the list, I will summarize.

Joerg Bruehe
