The issue with SRM and the Adaptec is booting from it. You can't. You
would need an SRM supported SCSI card (like the QLogic John mentioned).
But, once booted, you should be able to have "data" drives connected to
it just fine.

Or, use MILO from AlphaBios to boot Linux and you don't need a second
SCSI controller.

Also, the TGA2 cards are supported by the latest XFree86 releases these
days so you don't need to get another graphics card either.

