 Changing Default Screen from AlphaBIOS to SRM
 Go into AlphaBIOS setup by pressing F2, and
 then scroll down to CMOS
 settings. Hit Enter .Be sure that Parity is set
 to "Disabled
 & then hit
 F6
 (advanced setup)

 Tab down to "Console Selection" and choose
 your desired Operating System.

 Hit F10 twice and Power-Cycle your system.

 Wait for 30 seconds, and then restart.

 You should then see a blue screen that with a
 header stating your machine type with three chevrons.

 If your Alpha starts back up into the
 AlphaBIOS, do not worry - this means
 your battery is dead. These can be replaced for
 $5.00 either from us or from
 a Radio Shack or other good electronics store (use CR2032
 battery or equivelent)

 SRM Setup

 You may need to change a few parameters in the SRM
 console as follows:

 For OpenVMS

 >>>set boot_osflags 0,0
 >>>set os_type OpenVMS
 >>>set kbd_hardware_type LK411   (if you have a VMS
 style Keyboard)
 >>>set boot_reset OFF
