On Wed, Sep 26, 2001 at 03:47:05PM +0200, Heid Oliver wrote:
> I just tried the new 2.4.10 kernel (RH7.1 on UP2000+), and got one problem
> (so far): netscape fails with a mapping error on libXmu.so. A 2.4.9 kernel
> compiled with identical configs works fine. Does anybody have a fix?

I think it was caused by incomplete merging with Alan's tree.
Here is a fix.

Ivan.

--- 2.4.10/mm/mmap.c	Fri Sep 21 14:49:18 2001
+++ linux/mm/mmap.c	Fri Sep 21 16:58:51 2001
@@ -600,8 +600,11 @@ static inline unsigned long arch_get_unm
 		if (TASK_SIZE - len >= addr &&
 		    (!vma || addr + len <= vma->vm_start))
 			return addr;
+		if (addr > TASK_UNMAPPED_BASE)
+			addr = 0;
 	}
-	addr = PAGE_ALIGN(TASK_UNMAPPED_BASE);
+	if (!addr)
+		addr = PAGE_ALIGN(TASK_UNMAPPED_BASE);
 
 	for (vma = find_vma(current->mm, addr); ; vma = vma->vm_next) {
 		/* At this point:  (!vma || addr < vma->vm_end). */




