Hi all,
OK, now that the first bugs of 2.4.10. are out, we can go on ;-) In fact, I 
suspect that I still see the same bug as with the beginning of the 2.4's. I 
miss my PCI_QUIRKS setting. The kernel did OK for about an hour or two (with 
netscape ;-), but then all of a sudden my whole machine freezed. No ping, 
nothing.
 As I always had some trouble with the network (3c905B) under heavy load, I 
found out that only PCI_QUIRKS fixes it. But this doesn't exist under 2.4 
anymore. So after 2 hours of mp3s over my network, the computer hung. Just 
like this.
 Under a 2.2 I can go on for hours (never tried days, though). Only the 
X-server hangs from time to time. But with a rlogin this can be fixed. So, is 
it possible to get back the PCI_QUIRKS or should it be already in the kernel?

greets

ineiti




