XFree version is 4.0.3-21 from Redhat on a UP2000, one processor,
667 MHz.  Currently, it takes around 15 seconds from issuing
"startx" to actual server start.  The system is standalone, no
NFS or other implicit network latencies.

Formerly, using RH7.0 and a rawhide version of XFree 4.0.3, the X
server started fairly reliably in less than 5 seconds.  Even a
lowly 16-20MHz Sun 386i over a dozen years ago would start an X
server in much less time than it's now taking under RH7.1.

Is this slow start time inherent in RH7.1 and XFree 4.0.3-21, or
are there ways to speed it up?

Thanks.

