In my case, I'm not (knowingly) using KDE or Gnome, just plain
old X, using TWM as a window manager.  X startup fires up two
xterms, two xclocks, an xload, and an xcpustate.  It also does an
xmodmap (to get rid of the evil caps-lock key).  Under RH6.1 and
7.0, X server startup was less than 5 seconds.  With RH7.1, it
sometimes takes more than 15 seconds.  It appears that it's the
actual X server that is taking so long, independent of the
clients.

Robert Riches
