When it shows the graphics card information, is that the notice
of emulation of the card's X86 BIOS?  What card are you using?

I'm using an nVidia TNT2 Vanta, and I never see the BIOS
emulation message.  My script fires up startx in background
(stdout/stderr directed to a log file), sleeps 15 seconds, then
exits to free up the virtual console (and eliminate a security
hole of an unlocked text-mode virtual console session waiting to
be abused).  When it takes longer than 15 seconds for the X
server to start, the log file from startx says

    Authentication failed - cannot start X server.
    Perhaps you do not have console ownership?

This seems to imply the X server itself did not start until after
the 15 seconds had elapsed and the text-mode session had
terminated.  (I could increase the timeout to 20 or 30 or 60 or
90 or 3600 seconds, but waiting isn't fun.)

Robert Riches
richesr1@inetarena.com


