On Thu, Sep 27, 2001 at 09:44:54AM -0700, Robert M. Riches Jr. wrote:
> Since installing RH7.1, the X server is very slow to start.
> XFree version is 4.0.3-21 from Redhat on a UP2000, one processor,
> 667 MHz.  Currently, it takes around 15 seconds from issuing
> "startx" to actual server start.

Most likely this is not really your X server but you are using
a default kernel which was included in 7.1 distribution.  You will
notice that with it _anything_ which requires bigger amounts of memory
starts very slooowly and, even worse, runs this way.  For some reasons
the effect is much more pronounced on Alpha than on x86 although it
is present there as well.  I _think_ that very well known deficiencies
in VM handling, which are really bad in this kernel, show up in this
manner.  If this is the case then a slowdown may depend on amounts
of physical memory, virtual memory and your mix of applications.

If you do not want to experiment with kernels you compiled yourself
then I would strongly advise to replace this really unfortunate
kernel with something from the recent "rawhide" for Alpha (although
I do not have handy URL of mirrors which carry that).  Other than
that 2.4.9-ac10 should give a good base for further experiments.
2.4.10 plus a patch Ivan posted to handle COFF binaries is also
likely an interesting candidate (some later fixes from Andrea
should be taken into a consideration as well).

  Michal




