The reason I mentioned yesterday, explicitely, 2.4.9-ac10 and
2.4.10 (plus subsequent fixes) was that _both_ have different VM
handling than "older" mainline.  Methods employed by these two are
also not the same and more experience is needed with different
systems and different loads but so far they look like an essential
improvement over 2.4.3.

Saying that my experience with precompiled "rawhide" binaries
indicate that these are also provide a marked improvement (which
probably was not that hard as likely anything was an improvement :-)
over this unfortunate 2.4.3-2. YMMV but the first time I booted
that one I had a distinct impression that my machine just stopped
and which was only countered by grinding noises from disks.

  Michal




